288
00:30:59.131 --> 00:31:00.091
Requirements.

289
00:31:01.441 --> 00:31:02.764
R1, Erasure.

290
00:31:03.044 --> 00:31:16.975
A verified erasure request makes the customer's personal data unrecoverable in every store, including backups and the warehouse, within 30 days; legally retained records are kept under a separate key with minimum fields.

291
00:31:17.255 --> 00:31:19.004
R2, No stray PII.

292
00:31:19.284 --> 00:31:28.159
Zero card numbers and zero unapproved personal identifiers in logs and exports; findings alert the owning team within 1 hour.

293
00:31:28.439 --> 00:31:29.889
R3, Residency.

294
00:31:30.169 --> 00:31:39.791
Payment data and full replicas of localised stores exist only in Indian regions; every data flow passes the policy check before deploy.

295
00:31:40.071 --> 00:31:41.308
R4, Purpose.

296
00:31:41.588 --> 00:31:47.753
Every flow of personal data carries a purpose that matches consent or a documented legitimate use.

297
00:31:49.103 --> 00:31:50.938
R5, Audit integrity.

298
00:31:51.218 --> 00:31:59.175
Privileged actions are recorded in a tamper-evident log; verification runs hourly; the unanchored window is at most 1 minute.

299
00:31:59.455 --> 00:32:00.863
R6, Evidence.

300
00:32:01.143 --> 00:32:08.333
Policy results, scanner reports, key destructions and audit verifications are retained and reportable on demand.

301
00:32:08.613 --> 00:32:10.021
Decisions in detail.

302
00:32:10.301 --> 00:32:13.031
Classification (ADR-220).

303
00:32:13.311 --> 00:32:21.503
Seven classes (§2.3); schema annotations generate catalog entries; every store has an owner and retention.

304
00:32:22.853 --> 00:32:24.837
Keys (ADR-221).

305
00:32:25.117 --> 00:32:36.445
Envelope encryption: per-customer data keys wrapped by a KMS key; personal fields encrypted in the service before any write; search indexes store pseudonymous tokens.

306
00:32:36.725 --> 00:32:38.795
Logs (ADR-222).

307
00:32:39.075 --> 00:32:46.712
Logging library only emits allow-listed fields; scanner runs on the log pipeline and on exports, key-aware (L2).

308
00:32:46.992 --> 00:32:51.323
Residency (ADR-223 or 224).

309
00:32:51.603 --> 00:32:57.491
Manifest of data flows in the repo; rules in code; CI blocks violations (L3).

310
00:32:57.771 --> 00:32:59.499
DR region Hyderabad.

311
00:32:59.779 --> 00:33:02.232
Payments (ADR-225).

312
00:33:02.512 --> 00:33:07.867
Aggregator hosted checkout and network tokens; the platform never receives card numbers.

313
00:33:09.217 --> 00:33:11.649
Audit (ADR-226).

314
00:33:11.929 --> 00:33:19.054
Chain head anchored every minute to an Object-Lock bucket in a security-owned account; hourly verification (L4).

315
00:33:19.334 --> 00:33:22.086
Retention (ADR-227).

316
00:33:22.366 --> 00:33:34.547
Debug logs 14 d; app logs 90 d; security logs 180 d in India; GST invoices 72 months+; marketing data until consent withdrawn.

317
00:33:34.827 --> 00:33:35.851
Consequences.

318
00:33:36.131 --> 00:33:49.785
Encryption adds latency and complexity (key management, re-encryption on rotation, search over pseudonymous tokens); a second Indian region costs more than Singapore; engineers lose free-form logging.

319
00:33:50.065 --> 00:33:58.662
In return: erasure is provable, residency is enforced by construction, audit evidence is trustworthy, and audits become reports.

